abstract: >-
  FORRT computational reproduction of Vogelbacher et al. (2026, NHESS 26:2765-2783):
  the authors' building-level pluvial flood risk for their synthetic Hamburg
  city-quarter example (37 buildings, Zenodo 10.5281/zenodo.19860733) is
  recomputed with an independent open Python implementation instead of ArcGIS
  and compared building by building with the authors' output. Social
  vulnerability is reproduced exactly and every building falls in the same risk
  class for both risk indices. The FAIR2Adapt urban_pfr toolbox is also run as
  is, for comparison.
